I've written the Day 251 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The commit step ends in || true, so it was allowed to fail, and the planner can read the file from disk.

State: the harness had already checked that build and tests pass on 269a5561. In my own checks, yoyo -p answered "pong" and exited 0, and config get model read the right value. The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts, and the last 4 evolve runs succeeded.

What the planner should look at first:
1. #1012: an owner decision nobody has acted on. On 2026-11-03 @yuanhao wrote: "stop keeping a price table of your own… Reuse yoagent's pricing and delete yoyo's table." git log --grep '#1012' shows 0 commits since then. yoyo's own table (builtin_model_pricing, about 340 lines in src/format/cost.rs, plus promo, xai_region and bedrock_region) is still in place, and yoagent 0.27.1 already has the pricing functions to replace it (prices::enable_bundled, enable_live_cached, PriceTable::cost(provider, id)). The catch to plan around: yoagent looks prices up by provider plus model id, while yoyo looks them up by model id alone with the router prefix stripped. There are 13 callers of yoyo's lookup outside the cost module.
2. #1094: yoagent 0.27 now has `ReadLog`, which says it was modelled on yoyo's partial-read guard, and yoyo doesn't use it. src/tools.rs (around line 1391) builds the read and write tools with read_log: None.
3. Two files near the module-size limit. src/config.rs can grow 11 more lines and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs 14 more before cargo test fails outright, which reverts the whole task. A task that touches either file has to update its count in tests/module_size.rs in the same change.
4. Smaller open issues:
   • #1143: /add and --image still accept GIF files, which yoagent 0.27's read_file refuses.
   • #1114: yoyo -p --print-system-prompt prints the system prompt instead of sending it as the prompt.
   • #1026: the json and stream-json modes still don't print a note when a reply was cut off.

Research: Claude Code 2.1.318 (Nov 4) fixed claude -p reporting success when an API error cut off a reply, which is the same problem as #1026. Codex is testing the July 2026 MCP revision over streamable HTTP. yoyo has no HTTP MCP transport at all, and that is still its biggest structural gap against both. I saved one note on this to yopedia; its ingest job was queued.
